A `frontmatter-update` hook types its values exactly as the `frontmatter-update` CLI does:
`key=null` clears the key to a YAML null, booleans and integers are written unquoted,
and a string whose plain form would reload as another type stays quoted.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: parked
    statuses:
      parked:
        transitions:
          - to: resumed
            when: the run returns
            hooks: ["frontmatter-update return_to=null attempts=2 blocked=false label=plain answer=yes"]
      resumed: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: parked
return_to: inbox
---
-- cmd --
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks resumed --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
parked → resumed
frontmatter: status=resumed
frontmatter: return_to=null attempts=2 blocked=false label=plain answer=yes
-- stderr --
